# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the ASan-built (Debug) compiler and for
# programs built with `tspp --asan`. tests/run.sh and test.sh pass this file
# via LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...; `TSPP_LEAK_CHECK=1 tests/run.sh` fails
# on any unsuppressed leak in the compiler.
#
# Only genuine third-party leaks belong here (Boehm GC, LLVM internals, libc),
# one narrow entry per leak, each with a comment saying what leaks and why it
# is not ours. Never suppress malloc/calloc/realloc/operator new or broad
# llvm:: names: those match every allocation and hide every leak.
#
# Currently empty on purpose: with no suppressions, TSPP_LEAK_CHECK=1
# tests/run.sh reports no leaks (LLVM 23 + GCC 16 locally; LLVM 18 + GCC 13
# in CI), and the --asan builds of the run tests report none either.
